<section class="section deployment-question" id="build-the-system-develop-the-judgment-to-guide-it">
<div class="section-head">
<h2>Build the system. Develop the judgment to guide it.</h2>
</div>
<div class="section-body">
<p>As an agent moves from a demonstration towards operation, the questions become more consequential. What is it authorised to do? How do you know a task completed? What should happen when an action fails or a retry would repeat completed work?</p>
<p>This programme brings those questions into a scoped learning project. You work through the system, explain the design choices and revise through evaluation, review and continuous feedback.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section class="section deployment-fit" id="who-this-programme-is-for">
<div class="section-head">
<h2>Who this programme is for</h2>
</div>
<div class="section-body">
<ul>
<li>Experienced engineers who want to work through a broader agentic-system project.</li>
<li>Architects who want to examine decisions across the system&#x27;s operating path.</li>
<li>Engineering managers and directors who want deeper technical judgment for guiding a team.</li>
</ul>
<p>Fit depends on your starting capability, the project scope and the independent work you can commit to. Discuss those before joining.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section class="section deployment-process" id="what-you-work-through">
<h2>What you work through</h2>
<div class="deployment-chapters">
<nav aria-label="Project stages">
<a href="#define-the-problem-and-operating-boundaries">
<span aria-hidden="true">01</span>Define the problem and operating boundaries</a>
<a href="#design-the-architecture">
<span aria-hidden="true">02</span>Design the architecture</a>
<a href="#build-and-evaluate-the-system">
<span aria-hidden="true">03</span>Build and evaluate the system</a>
<a href="#take-the-project-through-deployment">
<span aria-hidden="true">04</span>Take the project through deployment</a>
<a href="#review-the-operating-decisions">
<span aria-hidden="true">05</span>Review the operating decisions</a>
</nav>
<div>
<article id="define-the-problem-and-operating-boundaries">
<span class="chapter-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
<h3>Define the problem and operating boundaries</h3>
<p>Establish the system&#x27;s purpose, the evidence of useful work and the actions it may take. Examine ownership and where human review belongs.</p>
</article>
<article id="design-the-architecture">
<span class="chapter-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
<h3>Design the architecture</h3>
<p>Connect the agent, tools, context and workflow. Review the trade-offs and explain how the design supports the intended behaviour.</p>
</article>
<article id="build-and-evaluate-the-system">
<span class="chapter-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
<h3>Build and evaluate the system</h3>
<p>Implement a working learning project. Examine useful results, failures and uncertain outcomes so you can revise the design using evidence.</p>
</article>
<article id="take-the-project-through-deployment">
<span class="chapter-number" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
<h3>Take the project through deployment</h3>
<p>Deploy the scoped project in an agreed learning environment. Review how the workflow completes, how failures are handled and what can be observed about its operation.</p>
</article>
<article id="review-the-operating-decisions">
<span class="chapter-number" aria-hidden="true">05</span>
<h3>Review the operating decisions</h3>
<p>Examine reliability, authority and cost alongside the working result. Identify the limits of the project and the further requirements an organisation would need to address.</p>
</article>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<div class="deployment-takeaway">
<div class="section deployment-summary">
<section id="what-you-leave-with">
<h2>What you leave with</h2>
<p>A working learning project taken through deployment, with clearer reasoning about its architecture and operating trade-offs. The project gives you practical work to review and explain; the discussions develop the judgment needed to guide similar decisions.</p>
</section>
<section class="deployment-time" id="your-time-commitment">
<h2>Your time commitment</h2>
<ul>
<li>
<strong>Live cohort work:</strong> {o.hours} hours with Sunil.</li>
<li>
<strong>Independent work:</strong> {o.independentWork}.</li>
<li>
<strong>Schedule:</strong> Discussed and agreed before joining.</li>
</ul>
<p>The independent work is additional to the live hours. Use it to build, evaluate and revise your project between discussions.</p>
</section>
</div>
</div>
<section class="section deployment-teacher" id="learn-with-sunil-mathew">
<div class="section-head">
<h2>Learn with Sunil Mathew</h2>
</div>
<div class="section-body">
<p>Sunil brings {EXPERIENCE}. His work with engineering teams informs how the programme examines architecture, evaluation and decisions with operating consequences.</p>
<p>The focus is practical capability: a working system and reasoning you can explain under review.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section class="section faq" id="questions-about-this-programme">
<h2>Questions about this programme</h2>
<div>
<details>
<summary>What does deployment mean here?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span>
</summary>
<div class="answer">
<p>It means taking an agreed learning project through deployment in an agreed learning environment. Adoption in an employer&#x27;s production environment requires that organisation&#x27;s own engineering, security, access and operating review.</p>
</div>
</details>
<details>
<summary>Can I bring a use case from my organisation?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span>
</summary>
<div class="answer">
<p>You can discuss a use case during the fit conversation. Its scope, data and access requirements need to be suitable for the learning programme.</p>
</div>
</details>
<details>
<summary>How is this different from the POC programme?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span>
</summary>
<div class="answer">
<p>
<a href="/programmes/agentic-systems/design-and-build-a-poc/">Design and Build a POC</a> centres on developing and evaluating a proof of concept. This programme adds deployment of the learning project and deeper discussion of its operating decisions.</p>
</div>
</details>
<details>
<summary>Can my organisation arrange a programme for a team?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span>
</summary>
<div class="answer">
<p>Yes. <a href="/programmes/agentic-systems/#discuss-your-team">Discuss a team programme</a> so its capability needs, scope, group size, schedule and fee can be considered separately.</p>
</div>
</details>
</div>
</section>
